{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_143","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"snapshot_stale_suffix.json\", \"summary\": \"Trace + bounded execution now submitted for follower snapshot catch-up. Question: after a follower handles an InstallSnapshotRequest while its own persisted log already ends *above* the snapshot's LastLogIndex, can it ever accept the leader's subsequent consistency check? Sources show it cannot: installSnapshot (raft.go:1814-1953, post-restore block 1930-1948) sets lastApplied/lastSnapshot/configuration and compacts only logs at or below req.LastLogIndex, but never truncates the suffix above it and never calls setLastLog. getLastEntry (state.go:167-174) therefore keeps returning the stale (lastLogIndex,lastLogTerm), so the AppendEntries PrevLogEntry check (raft.go:1475-1502) rejects (missing entry or stale term, NoRetryBackoff), replicateTo drives nextIndex down by one (replication.go:222-260) until setupAppendEntries hits ErrLogNotFound, and sendLatestSnapshot re-transfers the identical snapshot (replication.go:299-383) — a repeated, resource-amplifying progress stall rather than convergence.\\n\\nLocal native feedback (not the formal receipt) on the submitted harness `snapshot_suffix_harness.go`: in one process, 3 real Raft instances over InmemTransport/InmemStore/FileSnapshotStore with TrailingLogs=0. Control (`control_catchup`, isolated last index 25 < snapshot index 45): exactly one install, follower applied index reaches leader commit 55, stalled=false, isolated_caught_up=true. Case (`case_no_progress`, isolated last index 223 > snapshot index 45, produced by real uncommitted Apply calls on the old leader): follower applied index frozen at 45 across a 3s sample while leader commit is 55, stalled=true, isolated_caught_up=false; an earlier instrumented variant counted ~1430 repeated InstallSnapshot creates in 4s. The control isolates the stale-suffix condition as the cause.\\n\\nSubmitted one envelope (`draft/snapshot_stale_suffix.json`, validation.command reports valid=true): 9 source ranges, 5 verified code anchors, 1 investigation, 4 behavior statements, and 1 experiment with prerequisites on a distinct `scenario_setup` admission event and three comparisons. Draft harness file: `draft/snapshot_suffix_harness.go`. No interpretation/verdict is claimed yet — that awaits the controller's retained execution receipt for this experiment. Scope note: non-monotonic InmemStore path only; restart/recovery consequences and any safety (vs. progress) impact are untested.\"}"}}
